-- @ends-because vouches for a definition's recursion; above anything else it is a
-- check error naming what it sits on, and with no reason after it the mark is
-- refused too, because the reason is what a reader checks.
-- Errors expected, one each: the DECLARE, the ASSUME, the section heading, the
-- directive, a mark on a definition's GIVEN line (which names the input), the
-- empty reason on a top-level definition, and the empty reason on a WHERE local.
-- The marks above the two definitions with reasons are fine.

@ends-because the name is only a label
DECLARE Person HAS name IS A STRING

@ends-because the answer is supplied
ASSUME `is adult` IS A BOOLEAN

@ends-because each step is nearer the end
`can vote` MEANS `is adult`

@ends-because the heading is not a definition
§ `Part Two`
    GIVEN `is resident` IS A BOOLEAN

@ends-because each step is nearer the end
`can stand` MEANS `is resident`

@ends-because a directive is not a definition
#EVAL `can vote`

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN @ends-because the input is not a definition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`signature marked` MEANS x

@ends-because
`no reason given` MEANS `is resident`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`outer` n MEANS
  `inner` n
  WHERE
    @ends-because
    GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    `inner` k MEANS IF k EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `inner` (k MINUS 1)
